This repository contains the source code, profiles, assets, and modern build system
for the Stream Deck Discord Volume Mixer plugin (the "Software").

The Software is source-available, NOT open source. The source is published so that anyone
can read, build, and audit exactly what the plugin does. Publishing it does not place it in the
public domain and does not grant permission for unauthorized redistribution or re-publishing.


1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   a) Use it. You may install and use an official build of the Software, as published by
      the copyright holder, for your own personal, non-commercial purposes, for as long as
      you like and at no cost.

   b) Read & Build it. You may view, read, study, and compile the source code in this
      repository for your own personal use.

   c) Fork it on GitHub, for review only. Because this repository is public, GitHub's
      Terms of Service permit other GitHub users to fork it. That is acknowledged here.
      Such a fork may be used only to read, review, audit, or prepare a contribution.
      Every restriction in section 2 continues to apply to the contents of any fork.

   d) Contribute. You may open issues and submit pull requests. See section 4.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:

   a) Redistribute the Software, in source or built form, in whole or in part.

   b) Publish the Software, or anything derived from it, to any app store, marketplace,
